Implemented self-contained `../attempt/solve.py:1`.

- Exact prescribed FFT noise generation and discrete covariance.
- Adaptive eighth-order integration of spins and full oscillator memory, without Gilbert damping.
- Analytic checks, 12 numerical regimes, initialization checks, and CLI output validation pass.
- The 46,656-spin stiff benchmark completes in 32.3 seconds, below approximately 165 MiB peak memory.

Limitations: this models the specified finite-band bath acting on classical unit spins—not a full quantum many-spin system. Extreme stiffness can still exceed the runtime allowance. Details are in `../attempt/README.md:1`.
